{"text": " Thirty-three men, seven hundred metres underground, and nobody knew they were alive. On August 5th, 2010, a gold and copper mine in the Chilean desert collapsed. The miners crawled into a small emergency shelter. They had food for two or three days. They made it last two weeks. Up top, rescuers drilled blind, hole after hole. For 17 days, nothing. Then one drill came back up with a note stuck to it. We are fine in the refuge, the 33. That narrow hole became a lifeline. Water, food and letters went down in tubes. But to get the men out, the rescuers needed a shaft wide enough for a person, and a narrow steel capsule painted in the colours of Chilli's flag. Each ride up took about 15 minutes. On October 13, after 69 days, the last man, Luis Ursua, stepped out into the night. All 33 survived. Subscribe for more rescues.", "words": [{"word": "Thirty", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.32}, {"word": "-three", "start": 0.32, "end": 0.68}, {"word": "men,", "start": 0.68, "end": 1.02}, {"word": "seven", "start": 1.52, "end": 1.72}, {"word": "hundred", "start": 1.72, "end": 2.06}, {"word": "metres", "start": 2.06, "end": 2.48}, {"word": "underground,", "start": 2.48, "end": 3.14}, {"word": "and", "start": 3.48, "end": 3.94}, {"word": "nobody", "start": 3.94, "end": 4.34}, {"word": "knew", "start": 4.34, "end": 4.74}, {"word": "they", "start": 4.74, "end": 4.98}, {"word": "were", "start": 4.98, "end": 5.14}, {"word": "alive.", "start": 5.14, "end": 5.56}, {"word": "On", "start": 6.6, "end": 6.72}, {"word": "August", "start": 6.72, "end": 7.04}, {"word": " 5,", "start": 7.04, "end": 7.78}, {"word": "2010,", "start": 7.78, "end": 8.28}, {"word": "a", "start": 8.72, "end": 8.86}, {"word": "gold", "start": 8.86, "end": 9.14}, {"word": "and", "start": 9.14, "end": 9.34}, {"word": "copper", "start": 9.34, "end": 9.6}, {"word": "mine", "start": 9.6, "end": 9.88}, {"word": "in", "start": 9.88, "end": 10.12}, {"word": "the", "start": 10.12, "end": 10.26}, {"word": "Chilean", "start": 